# `joins: boolean | undefined`, `quiet: boolean | null`, each in one byte: the byte is the low byte of the value, whichever of true, false, undefined and null it is: the read gives the value as it lies, and its truth is one compare.
# A look that asked for a boolean there sent every object whose field holds undefined to the read by name. `strict: boolean`, `loud: boolean`: the source says that neither undefined nor null is read: a boolean is asked for as before.
# f1 = joined, f2 = hushed
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: : undefined|null|boolean @JSValue = GetSlot {{*}}key="joins" receivers=[L0] level=Proven
# CHECK: = ToBoolean {{*}}form=Bits
# CHECK: : boolean @Boolean = GetSlot {{*}}key="strict" receivers=[L0] level=Proven [holdsDeclaredType]
# RUN(NULL): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# NULL-LABEL: code f2:Body
# NULL: : undefined|null|boolean @JSValue = GetSlot {{*}}key="quiet" receivers=[L0] level=Proven
# NULL: = ToBoolean {{*}}form=Bits
# NULL: : boolean @Boolean = GetSlot {{*}}key="loud" receivers=[L0] level=Proven [holdsDeclaredType]
# RUN(LOOK): walk f1 f2 mechanisms=all
# LOOK-NOT: key="joins" {{*}}[holdsDeclaredType]
# LOOK-NOT: key="quiet" {{*}}[holdsDeclaredType]
# RUN(PLAN): plan layouts mechanisms=all
# PLAN: "joins" OptionalBoolean
# PLAN: "strict" OptionalBoolean
# PLAN: "quiet" OptionalBoolean
# PLAN: "loud" OptionalBoolean
# -- source: a-boolean-slot-written-with-undefined-is-asked-only-whether-it-is-filled.ts
